Why would I say this if I step out?

550
00:38:17,108 --> 00:38:18,942
What's in it for me?

551
00:38:18,943 --> 00:38:22,071
Actually, not saying it
might benefit me more, right?

552
00:38:24,240 --> 00:38:25,783
If you pay me, I'll keep the secret.

553
00:38:28,578 --> 00:38:29,621
I mean...

554
00:38:31,748 --> 00:38:32,957
How much?

555
00:38:36,085 --> 00:38:38,004
Well, maybe one billion?

556
00:38:38,421 --> 00:38:40,547
Don't just throw out numbers.
Come on, be realistic.

557
00:38:40,548 --> 00:38:42,215
Do I even have that much money?

558
00:38:42,216 --> 00:38:43,343
Why wouldn't you?

559
00:38:44,469 --> 00:38:46,387
I know when I see that kind of money.

560
00:38:46,888 --> 00:38:47,846
Okay.

561
00:38:47,847 --> 00:38:49,974
Let's say we did have that money, right?

562
00:38:50,183 --> 00:38:51,267
If we give you that money,

563
00:38:51,726 --> 00:38:53,311
you're not going to keep that promise.

564
00:38:53,811 --> 00:38:55,021
I said I would...

565
00:38:55,521 --> 00:38:58,523
Yes, well, you could think that way.

566
00:38:58,524 --> 00:39:00,150
But in this kind of situation,

567
00:39:00,151 --> 00:39:01,861
we need to trust each other.

568
00:39:02,320 --> 00:39:03,154
Are you going to kill me?

569
00:39:04,405 --> 00:39:05,531
You're not.

570
00:39:05,823 --> 00:39:07,115
I know you're not that kind of person.

571
00:39:07,116 --> 00:39:08,283
What I'm saying is...

572
00:39:08,284 --> 00:39:09,369
Hold on, Dong-ki.

573
00:39:12,205 --> 00:39:13,331
Wait a second.

574
00:39:14,165 --> 00:39:14,915
Hello?

575
00:39:14,916 --> 00:39:17,251
Hey, I'm on my way to the building.

576
00:39:17,794 --> 00:39:19,544
Yi-gyeong is coming with her mom
to the building.

577
00:39:19,545 --> 00:39:20,921
I think she wants to sign the contract.

578
00:39:20,922 --> 00:39:21,672
Now?

579
00:39:21,673 --> 00:39:23,216
Yes, they're in a big hurry.

580
00:39:23,466 --> 00:39:25,634
Looks like you were right
about the redevelopment.

581
00:39:25,635 --> 00:39:27,844
Yes, I've told you several times.

582
00:39:27,845 --> 00:39:30,430
I kept on telling you not to sell it.

583
00:39:30,431 --> 00:39:31,849
Okay, I'll head over right now.

584
00:39:32,058 --> 00:39:33,684
Dong-ki, I'll be right back.

585
00:39:33,685 --> 00:39:35,185
Hey, we need to still talk.

586
00:39:35,186 --> 00:39:36,771
Think about your daughter!

587
00:39:38,690 --> 00:39:40,483
Think about your daughter's future.

588
00:39:41,526 --> 00:39:42,777
Will you become a murderer?

589
00:39:44,529 --> 00:39:45,862
Da-rae, right?

590
00:39:45,863 --> 00:39:49,450
What do you think she'll say
if she saw this?

591
00:39:51,744 --> 00:39:54,330
You'll be talking nonsense...
"Da-rae! Da-rae!"

592
00:40:01,212 --> 00:40:02,671
I'll get to the point.

593
00:40:02,672 --> 00:40:04,465
I offered 30% over market price.

594
00:40:05,675 --> 00:40:06,551
Why?

595
00:40:07,593 --> 00:40:08,553
Why do you ask?

596
00:40:08,678 --> 00:40:11,597
Why did you offer
above market price?

597
00:40:11,931 --> 00:40:14,017
So you know too.

598
00:40:15,518 --> 00:40:17,185
Well,

599
00:40:17,186 --> 00:40:20,106
people are really interested
in this building lately.

600
00:40:20,398 --> 00:40:22,691
It's too big a deal for you to handle.

601
00:40:22,692 --> 00:40:23,735
You should step back.

602
00:40:24,152 --> 00:40:25,653
I gave a good offer.

603
00:40:26,279 --> 00:40:28,488
Mom, what's wrong?

604
00:40:28,489 --> 00:40:32,159
I appreciate you taking care
of my daughter and son-in-law.

605
00:40:32,160 --> 00:40:34,786
Moving forward,
I'll make sure to watch your back,

606
00:40:34,787 --> 00:40:35,955
so just sell the building.

607
00:40:39,542 --> 00:40:40,960
BUILDING SALE AGREEMENT

608
00:40:47,550 --> 00:40:49,594
We don't have time,
so let's just sign it and wrap it up.

609
00:40:52,513 --> 00:40:53,722
But,

610
00:40:53,723 --> 00:40:54,682
about Hwal-sung...

611
00:40:54,974 --> 00:40:55,807
What?

612
00:40:55,808 --> 00:40:57,684
Did you know that Hwal-sung

613
00:40:57,685 --> 00:40:59,353
wanted this building?

614
00:41:05,318 --> 00:41:06,402
I want to

615
00:41:07,320 --> 00:41:09,489
hold onto this building a bit longer.

616
00:41:09,906 --> 00:41:12,784
There must be a reason people want it.

617
00:41:14,660 --> 00:41:17,455
You're taking
this person's goodwill for granted.

618
00:41:18,414 --> 00:41:20,416
You really have no idea
how the world works.

619
00:41:21,584 --> 00:41:23,210
I told you earlier,

620
00:41:23,211 --> 00:41:25,879
you're not cut out to handle this.

621
00:41:25,880 --> 00:41:26,964
Come on, Mom.

622
00:41:27,423 --> 00:41:30,050
Yes, I understand what you're saying.

623
00:41:30,051 --> 00:41:33,096
I think I should discuss this
with my wife first.

624
00:41:33,805 --> 00:41:36,056
But for you to be suddenly
pushing for this,

625
00:41:36,057 --> 00:41:37,432
I'm feeling a bit overwhelmed today.

626
00:41:37,433 --> 00:41:38,809
What was I pushing?

627
00:41:38,810 --> 00:41:40,478
I already offered 30% more.

628
00:41:41,646 --> 00:41:43,856
I didn't mean
to ask for that, though.

629
00:41:45,525 --> 00:41:47,150
You'll regret it.

630
00:41:47,151 --> 00:41:48,694
You won't be able to handle this.

631
00:41:52,365 --> 00:41:54,117
I'll make sure to put in the effort.

632
00:41:54,617 --> 00:41:56,868
I'm sorry.

633
00:41:56,869 --> 00:41:59,288
Let's talk about it again next time.

634
00:41:59,789 --> 00:42:01,665
We need some time to think too.

635
00:42:01,666 --> 00:42:02,541
Yes, Mom.

636
00:42:02,542 --> 00:42:04,335
This feels too rushed today.

637
00:42:07,463 --> 00:42:09,423
You people have no idea.

638
00:42:12,677 --> 00:42:14,678
Sorry, I'll go talk to my mom.

639
00:42:14,679 --> 00:42:16,888
- No, it's fine.
- No, it's okay.

640
00:42:16,889 --> 00:42:17,807
It's okay.

641
00:42:20,518 --> 00:42:21,477
Mom.

642
00:42:21,686 --> 00:42:22,687
Mom!

643
00:42:24,689 --> 00:42:26,149
Mom!

644
00:42:29,193 --> 00:42:30,778
Yes, we have to think it over.

645
00:42:34,574 --> 00:42:36,616
Mom!

646
00:42:36,617 --> 00:42:38,493
Consider other people's perspectives too!

647
00:42:38,494 --> 00:42:41,122
Do we really have to go this far?

648
00:42:42,290 --> 00:42:43,665
You clueless fool.

649
00:42:43,666 --> 00:42:45,418
That's why you get taken advantage of.

650
00:42:46,210 --> 00:42:47,085
What?

651
00:42:47,086 --> 00:42:48,629
I heard you paid off your husband's debt.

652
00:42:49,380 --> 00:42:51,424
Mom, how did you know that?

653
00:42:51,674 --> 00:42:53,217
You're such a foolish girl.

654
00:42:54,927 --> 00:42:56,720
Wait, so you knew and still didn't help?

655
00:42:56,721 --> 00:42:58,431
Why should I help with that?

656
00:43:00,766 --> 00:43:01,309
But...

657
00:43:02,310 --> 00:43:03,561
Jeez!

658
00:43:04,812 --> 00:43:05,688
Yes?

659
00:43:07,523 --> 00:43:09,650
Can we meet up later tonight?

660
00:43:10,443 --> 00:43:12,528
I have a favor to ask.

661
00:43:15,865 --> 00:43:16,616
Yes.

662
00:43:17,450 --> 00:43:18,284
Okay.

663
00:43:30,713 --> 00:43:31,631
What?

664
00:43:32,173 --> 00:43:34,008
You ruined me, Mom.

665
00:43:36,177 --> 00:43:37,220
Later on,

666
00:43:38,262 --> 00:43:41,098
you'll realize that your mom was right.

667
00:43:41,474 --> 00:43:42,557
No.

668
00:43:42,558 --> 00:43:44,810
I'll never become someone like you.

669
00:43:51,692 --> 00:43:53,652
Can this really work?

670
00:43:53,653 --> 00:43:55,446
Is there another way?

671
00:43:56,239 --> 00:43:57,781
Not exactly.

672
00:43:57,782 --> 00:43:59,242
But how about lowering the amount a bit?

673
00:44:01,827 --> 00:44:03,119
No.

674
00:44:03,120 --> 00:44:04,664
Let's just pay him what we owe.

675
00:44:04,872 --> 00:44:05,872
Fine.

676
00:44:05,873 --> 00:44:06,749
Let's do it that way.

677
00:44:10,586 --> 00:44:14,089
I, Oh Dong-ki,
along with Kim Seon and Gi Su-jong,

678
00:44:14,090 --> 00:44:17,510
were involved as accomplices in
the kidnapping case of Jeon Yi-gyeong

679
00:44:18,886 --> 00:44:21,222
and received money in return.

680
00:44:21,764 --> 00:44:26,769
I pledge not to disclose this fact
to any third party

681
00:44:28,896 --> 00:44:33,442
and will uphold my duty of confidentiality
with my life.

682
00:44:34,026 --> 00:44:35,069
Yes.

683
00:44:35,987 --> 00:44:37,488
We're done.

684
00:44:38,823 --> 00:44:41,450
If you break the promise,
we're all dead.

685
00:44:41,617 --> 00:44:43,327
Oh, I'll definitely keep it.

686
00:44:43,786 --> 00:44:47,038
A single stab and being locked up
for two days for one billion?

687
00:44:47,039 --> 00:44:48,124
That's a sweet deal.

688
00:44:55,631 --> 00:44:56,549
Huh?

689
00:45:00,386 --> 00:45:01,219
But...

690
00:45:01,220 --> 00:45:02,430
Yes, Yi-gyeong?

691
00:45:03,347 --> 00:45:04,432
What is it?

692
00:45:06,600 --> 00:45:10,145
I'm back. I have things to tell you too.

693
00:45:10,146 --> 00:45:12,523
You're in the basement, right?

694
00:45:22,575 --> 00:45:23,617
She came to see us.

695
00:45:24,118 --> 00:45:27,163
Stay right there. I'll be right out.

696
00:45:27,872 --> 00:45:29,039
- I'm going.
- Okay.

697
00:45:29,040 --> 00:45:29,999
Take care of things
and come back up.

698
00:45:32,501 --> 00:45:33,293
Help me!

699
00:45:33,294 --> 00:45:35,004
Hey, hey!

700
00:45:37,340 --> 00:45:39,883
Wait! What are you doing, Dong-ki?

701
00:45:39,884 --> 00:45:41,427
Do you really want to die? Huh?

702
00:46:01,572 --> 00:46:03,824
Dong-ki, my nose is bleeding!

703
00:46:05,785 --> 00:46:07,327
Yi-gyeong?

704
00:46:07,328 --> 00:46:09,120
Seon, did you hear something?

705
00:46:09,121 --> 00:46:10,081
Hear what?

706
00:46:10,373 --> 00:46:12,165
I think I heard someone shouting.

707
00:46:12,166 --> 00:46:16,169
This building is old, so sometimes,
sounds from the first floor come through.

708
00:46:16,170 --> 00:46:17,505
But what's going on?

709
00:46:18,005 --> 00:46:19,255
Well, you see.

710
00:46:19,256 --> 00:46:21,842
Can we talk quietly?

711
00:46:22,385 --> 00:46:24,011
Yeah, sure.

712
00:46:24,387 --> 00:46:26,472
- Should we go to the roof?
- Yes.

713
00:46:28,182 --> 00:46:30,768
I'm sorry. Can you untie this?

714
00:46:32,812 --> 00:46:34,270
Why won't this open?

715
00:46:34,271 --> 00:46:35,314
What? It won't open?

716
00:46:36,816 --> 00:46:38,067
You're in trouble now.

717
00:46:40,152 --> 00:46:42,529
What trouble? Come on, Dong-ki.

718
00:46:42,530 --> 00:46:43,989
Try to speak nicely.

719
00:46:44,198 --> 00:46:47,784
I have the key
to the handcuffs right here.

720
00:46:47,785 --> 00:46:48,536
Where is it?

721
00:46:49,161 --> 00:46:50,037
Hold on.

722
00:46:50,704 --> 00:46:51,329
Where did it go?

723
00:46:51,330 --> 00:46:51,789
It's not there?

724
00:46:52,957 --> 00:46:53,791
It's gone.

725
00:46:57,795 --> 00:46:58,754
Damn it!

726
00:46:59,588 --> 00:47:00,714
First of all,

727
00:47:01,507 --> 00:47:03,717
I'm sorry about my mom.

728
00:47:04,802 --> 00:47:07,095
It's not your fault, Yi-gyeong.

729
00:47:07,096 --> 00:47:08,096
Still,

730
00:47:08,097 --> 00:47:09,890
I set up the meeting.

731
00:47:11,183 --> 00:47:13,352
I'm really sorry and feel ashamed.

732
00:47:15,938 --> 00:47:17,481
That's just how family is.

733
00:47:19,191 --> 00:47:21,359
Though it's frustrating and embarrassing,

734
00:47:21,360 --> 00:47:22,736
you carry the burdens.

735
00:47:26,323 --> 00:47:28,701
I don't know why my life
turned out like this.

736
00:47:29,952 --> 00:47:32,954
Yi-gyeong, who lives as well as you do?

737
00:47:32,955 --> 00:47:34,707
Hwal-sung has a girlfriend.

738
00:47:36,250 --> 00:47:37,877
She's a married woman
with a kid.

739
00:47:38,502 --> 00:47:39,670
But Hwal-sung

740
00:47:43,424 --> 00:47:45,259
was talking bad about me with her.

741
00:47:46,469 --> 00:47:48,304
He said I'm empty inside,

742
00:47:49,555 --> 00:47:51,348
that I'm immature and have no charm.

743
00:47:54,393 --> 00:47:57,104
I guess he married
for our family's money, right?

744
00:47:57,605 --> 00:48:00,148
I'm just young, rich, and kind of dumb.

745
00:48:00,149 --> 00:48:01,901
I guess he thought, "What a steal!"

746
00:48:02,651 --> 00:48:04,528
No, Yi-gyeong.

747
00:48:06,405 --> 00:48:08,657
You're such a beautiful person.

748
00:48:11,118 --> 00:48:12,369
Yi-gyeong.

749
00:48:20,127 --> 00:48:21,337
Want to have a beer?

750
00:48:22,588 --> 00:48:23,297
Yes.

751
00:48:32,723 --> 00:48:34,183
Let go! let go of that!

752
00:48:41,524 --> 00:48:43,150
Stop it!

753
00:48:46,403 --> 00:48:48,988
Let go!

754
00:48:48,989 --> 00:48:51,366
Let go! Oh Dong-ki, let go!

755
00:48:51,367 --> 00:48:53,494
- My head!
- Su-jong is a real man.

756
00:48:54,161 --> 00:48:55,788
Huh? About what?

757
00:48:57,164 --> 00:48:58,832
He's sincere.

758
00:48:59,917 --> 00:49:01,001
Oh.

759
00:49:03,796 --> 00:49:05,588
Who could it be?

760
00:49:05,589 --> 00:49:06,882
The woman he cheated with.

761
00:49:08,342 --> 00:49:10,386
I thought I wouldn't be curious,

762
00:49:11,136 --> 00:49:13,555
but now that it's happening to me,

763
00:49:13,556 --> 00:49:15,224
I'm really curious about her

764
00:49:16,225 --> 00:49:18,601
and what kind of woman
could make Hwal-sung

765
00:49:18,602 --> 00:49:21,188
cheat with a married woman?

766
00:49:22,398 --> 00:49:23,941
I'm dying to know.

767
00:49:25,734 --> 00:49:26,986
Is she pretty?

768
00:49:27,945 --> 00:49:29,738
Is she sexy? Is she smart?

769
00:49:31,323 --> 00:49:32,616
It's not like that.

770
00:49:34,535 --> 00:49:35,160
What?

771
00:49:37,162 --> 00:49:38,789
It's just that

772
00:49:40,457 --> 00:49:43,460
some people don't realize
what they have is precious.

773
00:49:44,795 --> 00:49:47,255
When you're unhappy with reality,

774
00:49:47,256 --> 00:49:48,882
you covet what belongs to others.

775
00:49:49,675 --> 00:49:51,010
That's just human nature.

776
00:49:51,885 --> 00:49:53,553
What's better or worse

777
00:49:53,554 --> 00:49:56,307
doesn't seem that important.

778
00:49:57,891 --> 00:50:00,477
Yi-gyeong, it's not your problem.
It's Hwal-sung's problem.

779
00:50:05,107 --> 00:50:05,816
Seon.

780
00:50:07,234 --> 00:50:10,237
What books have you been reading
to make you talk so cool?

781
00:50:10,571 --> 00:50:12,156
Please tell me.

782
00:50:13,157 --> 00:50:15,450
Oh, what's so cool about it?

783
00:50:15,451 --> 00:50:17,744
- Okay, Dong-ki.
- Okay, I said I put it down!

784
00:50:17,745 --> 00:50:20,079
Then take a break. Let's rest.

785
00:50:20,080 --> 00:50:21,915
Let's rest.

786
00:50:24,668 --> 00:50:26,378
- Oh.
- Gosh.

787
00:50:30,674 --> 00:50:32,176
Do you remember that?

788
00:50:32,801 --> 00:50:34,136
Remember what?

789
00:50:35,721 --> 00:50:36,889
Nice landlord.

790
00:50:38,098 --> 00:50:38,932
During COVID?

791
00:50:39,391 --> 00:50:41,894
Yes, when I started my cafe back then.

792
00:50:43,687 --> 00:50:44,855
Oh, those were good times.

793
00:50:46,774 --> 00:50:48,817
I think the latte back then
was the best.

794
00:50:51,153 --> 00:50:53,447
- Yes...
- That time,

795
00:50:54,156 --> 00:50:55,699
you did it
for the tax benefits, right?

796
00:50:56,116 --> 00:50:58,494
Don't talk nonsense.
That's how the law normally is.

797
00:51:00,287 --> 00:51:01,372
What are you doing?

798
00:51:04,833 --> 00:51:06,834
Forget your law nonsense!

799
00:51:06,835 --> 00:51:08,420
That was quite the strategy.

800
00:51:08,754 --> 00:51:10,129
I got you, didn't I?

801
00:51:10,130 --> 00:51:12,924
Hey, Dong-ki, don't do this!
Hurry and let me go!

802
00:51:12,925 --> 00:51:15,636
Thanks so much
for your advice today.

803
00:51:15,886 --> 00:51:18,555
Oh, it's nothing.
Just let me know when you need help.

804
00:51:19,348 --> 00:51:21,475
Let's really meet often
from now on.

805
00:51:22,101 --> 00:51:23,560
Sure.

806
00:51:27,648 --> 00:51:28,649
Die!

807
00:51:29,400 --> 00:51:30,983
Die!

808
00:51:30,984 --> 00:51:32,069
Die! Damn it!

809
00:51:52,381 --> 00:51:53,882
What's going on? He didn't come out?

810
00:51:59,054 --> 00:52:00,305
What's wrong with this?

811
00:52:02,391 --> 00:52:03,308
Huh?

812
00:52:05,602 --> 00:52:07,603
What did I do so wrong?

813
00:52:07,604 --> 00:52:08,522
Honey!

814
00:52:09,231 --> 00:52:11,483
You think giving me money
will solve everything?

815
00:52:11,650 --> 00:52:12,901
Making me pee my pants!

816
00:52:13,318 --> 00:52:14,153
Die!

817
00:52:14,319 --> 00:52:15,195
Dong-ki, don't do this...

818
00:52:16,447 --> 00:52:17,238
Huh?

819
00:52:17,239 --> 00:52:18,698
Honey!

820
00:52:18,699 --> 00:52:19,658
Let's go!

821
00:52:21,368 --> 00:52:22,076
Jeez!

822
00:52:22,077 --> 00:52:23,036
Damn it!

823
00:52:59,364 --> 00:53:02,868
It's about doing
what we did before once more.

824
00:53:03,869 --> 00:53:05,870
You're saying to go to Seyoon Building

825
00:53:05,871 --> 00:53:07,498
and create building defects?

826
00:53:07,873 --> 00:53:09,625
It's not that hard.

827
00:53:10,417 --> 00:53:13,587
We just need to go and break a few pipes.

828
00:53:13,921 --> 00:53:15,297
Don't you think

829
00:53:15,756 --> 00:53:17,966
we're too old for that?

830
00:53:18,717 --> 00:53:20,511
We're better than those youngsters.

831
00:53:33,982 --> 00:53:35,234
Do we really have to go that far?

832
00:53:35,984 --> 00:53:39,112
If you knew the humiliation I faced today,

833
00:53:39,738 --> 00:53:41,573
you wouldn't say that.

834
00:53:49,456 --> 00:53:51,415
WHOEVER FINDS HIS LIFE WILL LOSE IT

835
00:53:51,416 --> 00:53:53,585
And whoever loses their life for my sake
will find it. Matthew 10:39

836
00:54:26,994 --> 00:54:28,745
I can lend you the equipment.

837
00:54:30,122 --> 00:54:31,874
But that's as far as it goes.

838
00:54:32,457 --> 00:54:34,585
You won't get your hands dirty?

839
00:54:35,168 --> 00:54:36,794
That landlord

840
00:54:36,795 --> 00:54:38,255
is someone I know too.

841
00:54:40,048 --> 00:54:41,800
I have my principles as well.

842
00:54:46,346 --> 00:54:47,389
Fine.

843
00:54:49,016 --> 00:54:51,643
It's easier for me to do it myself anyway.

844
00:54:52,603 --> 00:54:54,897
Dirty work, unpleasant tasks,
dangerous jobs,

845
00:54:55,689 --> 00:54:58,942
I've done them all myself to get here.

846
00:54:59,693 --> 00:55:00,527
Why?

847
00:55:02,321 --> 00:55:05,198
You can't trust a black-haired beast.

848
00:55:12,789 --> 00:55:14,082
You'll regret it.

849
00:55:16,001 --> 00:55:18,503
I've been regretting it
for a long time.

850
00:55:29,973 --> 00:55:31,183
That must hurt.

851
00:55:36,855 --> 00:55:38,231
Dong-ki will be okay, right?

852
00:55:38,815 --> 00:55:40,984
Yes, though he might be hurt a bit.

853
00:55:42,319 --> 00:55:43,277
All done.

854
00:55:43,278 --> 00:55:45,572
Gosh, what are we
supposed to do now?

855
00:55:46,323 --> 00:55:48,699
I don't know either.

856
00:55:48,700 --> 00:55:50,035
We'll just have to wait and see.

857
00:55:52,454 --> 00:55:54,705
When that punk Hwal-sung

858
00:55:54,706 --> 00:55:56,040
mentioned about kidnapping back then,

859
00:55:56,041 --> 00:55:58,293
I should have said no then.
I must have been crazy.

860
00:55:59,836 --> 00:56:01,713
I was just so focused
on protecting the building.

861
00:56:02,506 --> 00:56:03,632
That's not true.

862
00:56:04,508 --> 00:56:06,760
You still did your best.

863
00:56:07,594 --> 00:56:09,137
You did it for us.

864
00:56:11,848 --> 00:56:14,226
If I go to prison,
will you put in food for me?

865
00:56:18,480 --> 00:56:20,356
You think you're the only one going in?

866
00:56:20,357 --> 00:56:21,482
I should go in too.

867
00:56:21,483 --> 00:56:22,693
No, you can't.

868
00:56:23,151 --> 00:56:24,319
You have Da-rae to care for.

869
00:56:24,528 --> 00:56:26,487
She has to get surgery and go to college.

870
00:56:26,488 --> 00:56:27,656
She needs to get married.

871
00:56:28,323 --> 00:56:29,700
Just keep that money safe,

872
00:56:30,701 --> 00:56:31,952
then you can do it.

873
00:56:35,747 --> 00:56:37,082
We'll stick together till the end.

874
00:56:38,333 --> 00:56:40,543
No matter where we go,

875
00:56:40,544 --> 00:56:42,087
let's keep going together.

876
00:56:47,467 --> 00:56:48,677
We'll be okay, right?

877
00:56:51,346 --> 00:56:52,347
Yes.

878
00:58:46,419 --> 00:58:47,254
This is a whip!

879
00:59:01,017 --> 00:59:01,852
Oh, I'm sorry!

880
00:59:49,024 --> 00:59:52,109
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

881
00:59:52,110 --> 00:59:53,235
Is this all there is?

882
00:59:53,236 --> 00:59:55,821
Oh, we started using
the CCTV last night.

883
00:59:55,822 --> 00:59:58,240
It was off due to issues before that.

884
00:59:58,241 --> 01:00:00,451
Doesn't this situation
seem strange?

885
01:00:00,452 --> 01:00:02,329
The things only happening
in this building.

886
01:00:02,537 --> 01:00:03,621
Wake up!

887
01:00:03,622 --> 01:00:06,248
Are you scared
I'll get arrested or something?

888
01:00:06,249 --> 01:00:08,585
Bring me the money, okay?
Before I blow this whole thing up!

889
01:00:08,877 --> 01:00:10,419
When I was kidnapped,

890
01:00:10,420 --> 01:00:13,631
didn't you mention something
about the place I was held?

891
01:00:13,632 --> 01:00:15,758
Yi-gyeong asked
about the storage freezer?

892
01:00:15,759 --> 01:00:17,051
You're good at
finding people, right?

893
01:00:17,052 --> 01:00:18,093
I'm looking for that person.

894
01:00:18,094 --> 01:00:20,095
Oh, we can do anything
as long as we get paid.

895
01:00:20,096 --> 01:00:20,888
Get him!

896
01:00:20,889 --> 01:00:22,514
Are we suspects?

897
01:00:22,515 --> 01:00:25,226
If you hadn't made
that suggestion to me,

898
01:00:25,227 --> 01:00:26,645
we wouldn't be here.

